==Strategy==
Not a terribly difficult stage, but be prepared for the fight because it happens whether you're ready or not.

Obviously you'll want as many [[Treasure]]s as possible and you'll want to bring [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]], [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Aliens]] and something tanky enough to stop the Doge Dark pressure.

==='''Chapter 1'''===
Here, its simple but easy to mess up. Of course, as said earlier, you should get most ITF treasures beforehand, or else the Maawths will have 444K HP and deal 19K Damage per hit.

You don't need many Zombie Killers, as theres only Zoges and Znaches here, with a merely 150% magnificence. The Trolley Bloggers are a bit annoying, but a simple Area Attack rusher like [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]] will handle them. Stackable attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] or [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] shine here with a few meatshields.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Similar to Chapter 1, just be careful of The Thrillerz burrowing twice. Taking as much [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] power as possible is in your best interest. Anti-Alien units help with the Maawth as well.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Pick your toughest meatshield and spam it as soon as you have the cash for it. Forcing The Thrillerz to burrow ASAP is very important here and the Trolly Bloggers push your guys back very fast.

Once you've survived this initial wave, the Mooth/Maawth combo immediately spawns and they have a Li'l Zyclone in tow this time.

The Li'l Zyclone is clearly the biggest threat here as he burrows for over 1000 range and revives with his full health of 333,000. Deal with him as you would any other long-distance-burrower, by trying to force them to burrow as early as possible. Afterwards, the Cyclone does very little damage and acts more like a barrier between your units you already spawned and the units that are trying to catch up to them. Finish him quickly with heavy hitting Zombie Killers so your units don't get separated.

But wait, there's more! Once your first Li'l Zyclone dies, another one spawns along with a pair of Mooth/Maawth to help the ones you're probably already struggling to deal with. Keeping this Zyclone from burrowing is incredibly important. Due to the massive stream of stick figures, you can't really push forward at any point, so the [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast Cannon]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], a perfectly timed default [[Cat Cannon]], or [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]] could all be super helpful to push him back and keep him from getting past your line and all the way to your base.

If by chance the 2nd one does burrow, you can save your Cat Cannon and any crowd-controllers and spawn them as he starts to hit the [[Cat Base]]. His DPS isn't amazing, so you have time, but don't wait to try pushing him off your base.

Once the 2nd Li'l Zyclone is down, you have a 2-3 minute trek through the unyielding stick figure spawn rate. A couple more Mooths/Maawths will spawn to annoy you, but the real fight ends with the death of Zyclone #2.

